% S6: a transfer passenger only boards the second car at I after the first car dropped them there.
% NOT model-checked (decision 2026-10-21): the order holds by construction. A cross-wing request
% is one pool entry that is rewritten into its second leg only when the first car drops the
% passenger at I (afterVisit), so no second leg exists before that. A formula cannot express
% this: boarding is not an observable action, and the pool has no passenger identities.
% See docs/design.md section 6.1 and docs/questions.md question 1.
%
% Original draft (uses a request ID and pickup/dropoff actions that the model does not have):
%
% forall i: ReqId, o,d: Loc .
%   val(crossWing(o,d)) =>
%     [true* . request(i,o,d) .
%       (!dropoff(i,carOf(o),o,I))* .
%        pickup(i,carOf(d),I,d)] false
